{
  "type": "skill",
  "slug": "anatomy",
  "name": "Anatomy",
  "description": "Build detailed, interactive isometric SVG figures that explain a technical idea as a real physical machine, with optional WebGL shaders and 3D.",
  "longDescription": "Ships a zero-dependency Node kit, **8 worked examples** and **8 references** for drawing explainer figures as dense isometric machines of 40–150 parts, with depth-ordered shading, a framed card and eased motion.\n\n- **Kit**: `iso-kit.mjs` core, `lathe.mjs` round parts, `tube.mjs` pipes and cables, `gl.mjs` WebGL shaders, `turn.mjs` 3D mode (beta), React components\n- **Checks**: `audit.mjs` geometry audit, `lines.mjs` line-end check, `capture.mjs` and `drive.mjs` headless Chrome screenshots\n- **Examples**: dial indicator, desk computer, arcade cabinet, Raptor engine, ripple tank, test rig, spot plate, turning dial\n\nNeeds Node 20.10 or later; the checks drive headless Chrome.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex",
    "opencode"
  ],
  "author": {
    "name": "Ryan",
